[00:12.10]1. Jehovah is our refuge,
[00:17.76]Our God in whom we trust.
[00:22.56]His shadow is our shelter;
[00:28.76]Remain in it we must.
[00:33.84]His faithful ones he will defend,
[00:40.18]On this we know we can depend.
[00:46.02]Jehovah is a stronghold,
[00:50.60]Ever faithful, loyal, and just.
[01:05.56]2. Though thousands will have fallen
[01:11.32]And many at our side,
[01:16.12]The righteous and the meek ones
[01:21.92]Will never be denied.
[01:27.48]So in our hearts we need not fear;
[01:34.66]Calamity will not come near.
[01:39.42]From danger he will shield us,
[01:44.24]For beneath God’s wings we’ll reside.
[02:24.16]3. He’ll keep us and protect us
[02:30.24]From snares along our way,
[02:35.90]From terrors in the nighttime,
[02:40.94]And arrows by the day.
[02:46.46]Yes, there will be no cause for dread,
[02:52.14]No place where we will fear to tread.
[02:58.70]Jehovah is our refuge,
[03:03.36]Ever guarding us on our way.
